course: dictionary
lesson: 4329
title: Gruff: how someone sounds
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Gruff is a word about a voice. A gruff voice is low, deep and rough, like a grumble. It can also describe a person who speaks shortly and seems a bit impatient. Read the words around gruff to find out which meaning fits.
explain: Look at this example: The Badger's first words are gruff: «Now, the very next time this happens, I shall be exceedingly angry.» The words are sharp and stern, so gruff tells you how Badger sounds when he speaks.
explain: A gruff person is not always unkind. In The Wind in the Willows, Badger speaks shortly and hates Society, but he is kind and wise, and he looks after Mole and Ratty in the snow. A gruff person can have a warm heart under a rough voice.
fact: Gruff means low, deep and rough, or rather unfriendly in the way someone speaks.
fact: Gruff can describe a voice: a gruff voice sounds like a grumble.
fact: A person who is gruff may be kind underneath.
fact: Gruffly is the adverb, and it means in a gruff way.
fact: In «The Three Billy Goats Gruff», the goats outwit the troll under the bridge.
exercise: The Badger's first words are gruff: «Now, the very next time this happens, I shall be exceedingly angry.» What does gruff tell you? | Where Badger lives | *How Badger sounds when he speaks | What Badger is eating | How old Badger is
exercise: A gruff voice is low, deep and rough. Which voice is gruff? | A soft, gentle whisper | A high, squeaky, giggling voice | *A low, rough, grumbling voice | A loud, happy song
exercise: Pick the word that means in a gruff way. | Gently | Quickly | *Gruffly | Sleepily
test: Can a gruff person be kind underneath? | Never, because gruff is a colour | No, gruff always means unkind | *Yes, they can be kind underneath | Only in fairy tales
test: In «The Three Billy Goats Gruff», what do the goats do to the troll? | *They outwit him | They sing him to sleep | They make him a cake | They ask him to dinner
exam: Which sentence uses gruff correctly? | She gruffed her favourite song loudly. | The gruff children ate their lunch in the garden. | The gruff sun shone brightly on the sea. | *The old man gave a gruff reply, but he helped us carry the boxes.
